From 0c534765fdccea186d5d0d75463a60c5ff3481fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven Lee <steven_lee@aspeedtech.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:27:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fw-update: support PLDM package format revision 1.3.0

Squashed backport of openbmc/pldm Gerrit change 93835 ("fw-update:
support package format revision 1.3.0", patchset 6) together with its
whole relation chain and the master commits it sits on, rebased onto the
pldm SRCREV pinned by meta-phosphor (ecb4b2bb) with the SDK's
0001-Add-back-maximum-transfer-size-configuration.patch already applied.

Carrying the chain as a single patch keeps the SDK on the stock pldm,
libpldm and sdbusplus revisions: no SRCREV override, no libpldm bbappend
and no sdbusplus compatibility shim are needed. libpldm 58463c9c already
ships the libpldm++ C++ bindings with v1_3_0 package support, and
sdbusplus 4e82142c already provides the top-level match aliases.

Squashed upstream commits (oldest first):

  039648e pldm: prefer empty() over size() == 0
  fef35d5 oem-ibm: Fix null buffer check in PCIeInfoHandler::write
  b109898 common/utils: use decoder in findStateSensorPDR
  2cd857d common/utils: use decoder in findStateSensorId
  cc8d016 fix build failure by reverting 2cd857d b109898
  283e1dd pldmd: fix unsupported command handling
  7dabc62 bios: add getValueIndex unit test coverage
  ea365dc fw_update: add pre-post update conditions
  4a48c52 fw-update/test: fix ComponentClassification            (92394, merged)
  dff776e package_parser: remove redundant pkg size param        (92432, merged)
  4e11a78 common/types.hpp: fix name conflict                    (92387)
  1546c7b migrate to libpldm++ PackageParser                     (92352)
  a47e4dc fw-update: sort descriptors before comparing           (93831)
  f9643e2 fw-update: widen RequestFirmwareData offsets           (93832)
  204b769 fw-update: hold component images as spans              (93833)
  ddc0e54 fw-update: restore component image validation          (93834)
  3acbf1e fw-update: support package format revision 1.3.0       (93835)

Conflict resolved during the rebase: 204b769 reintroduced the hardcoded
MAXIMUM_TRANSFER_SIZE constant in fw-update/update_manager.cpp that
0001-Add-back-maximum-transfer-size-configuration.patch removes; the
meson-configured value is kept.

Drop this patch once the SDK moves to an OpenBMC revision that already
carries Gerrit 93835.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/93835]
Signed-off-by: Steven Lee <steven_lee@aspeedtech.com>
